  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`src/evidence.rs#fn[validate_evidence_file]` is a site because it takes the parameter `errors: &mut Vec<String>`. It meets the obligations of `requirements.ci.errors`.\n\n**Early returns (the four `early_exits` violation matches).** Each `return` handles a failure to parse or decode the evidence file itself:\n- The `fs::read_to_string` failure reports \"cannot read evidence\".\n- The `serde_json::from_str` failure reports \"invalid JSON\".\n- The `crate::evidence_format::view` failure reports \"invalid evidence format\".\n- The `value.as_object()` failure reports \"expected a JSON object\".\n\nThe requirement says an unparseable file is one failed check. Its error MAY report only the first parse or decoding problem, and only checks that do not depend on the file's contents must still run. Every check after these returns reads the parsed object, so none is skipped improperly. `crate::evidence_format::check_native` runs before the object check, so the SDK freshness check is not skipped when only the object-shape check fails. None of these returns sits between two independent checks, so none breaks the rule.\n\n**Checks on a well-formed record.** After parsing, the function does not exit early. These checks run in sequence:\n- `check_keys`\n- the `references` digest format\n- the text field (empty, and changed against `expected`)\n- `determination` parsing, which reports a missing field or an invalid value and then continues with `None`\n- `rationale` emptiness\n- `determination` false\n- `validate_dependencies` for orphaned records\n- every `inputs[index]` through `validate_input` in a loop with no `continue` or `break`\n\nA failure in one check does not stop the later ones.\n\n**Duplicate reports.** Each failure is reported once.\n- Each field is read once through `string_field` or `array_field`.\n- `determination` has separate branches for missing and invalid, and the false-determination message is a separate condition.\n- `crate::evidence_format::check_native` deliberately drops the dependency observations that the application checks already explain. Its own comment says the application validators report the field-specific failures. It therefore adds only an SDK-version or dependency-changed finding.\n\nNo gap found.",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "file": "src/evidence.rs",
      "item": "fn[validate_evidence_file]",
      "hash": "a5b094bae2358675e9aecc733eb4ce8ebfd79a3a8a8af530eb394135b3aa8823"
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.ci.errors",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.ci.errors"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::::{req} errors",
        "Repository validation MUST continue after a failed check and report every failed",
        "check it finds in one run, each as a {term}`requirements.ci.validation_error`.",
        "This is a convention for every validation error; the requirement for each check",
        "states which conditions that check reports. A file that cannot be parsed, such as",
        "a malformed `habeas.toml`, `book.toml`, or evidence file, is one failed check:",
        "its error MAY report only the first parse or decoding problem in that file, and",
        "checks that do not depend on its contents MUST still run.",
        "",
        "The code that sequences the repository's checks carries out the first paragraph.",
        "A repository-validation function that collects validation errors MUST hold them",
        "in a parameter or local variable named `errors`, and a function with such a",
        "variable is a site below; authoring code that collects errors only to abort is",
        "not one. After one of its checks fails, a site MUST still run every later check",
        "that does not depend on the failed check's result, including later checks in the",
        "same loop iteration, and MUST NOT report one failure twice.",
        "",
        "::::{sites} error_accumulators",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src, crates/habeas-sdk/src]",
        "exclude: [src/authoring/inputs.rs, src/authoring/tools.rs]",
        "rule:",
        "  kind: function_item",
        "  has:",
        "    stopBy: { kind: function_item }",
        "    any:",
        "      - kind: parameter",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "      - kind: let_declaration",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "  not:",
        "    inside:",
        "      stopBy: end",
        "      kind: mod_item",
        "      has: { field: name, regex: \"^tests$\" }",
        "match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut errors: BTreeSet<String> = BTreeSet::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut errors);",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, discovery_errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut problems = Vec::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut problems);",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    mod tests {",
        "        fn check(errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        "",
        "::::{violations} early_exits",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src, crates/habeas-sdk/src]",
        "within: error_accumulators",
        "rule:",
        "  any:",
        "    - kind: try_expression",
        "    - kind: return_expression",
        "    - kind: continue_expression",
        "    - kind: break_expression",
        "match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); continue; }",
        "            if item.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        if !v.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); return; }",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); break; }",
        "        }",
        "        if items.is_empty() { errors.push(\"empty\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn parse(v: &Value) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        ":::::"
      ]
    },
